3) How Keycloak connected with API Gateway + Spring Security (Salam-style)
═══════════════════════════════════════

In a Salam-like microservices setup, Keycloak is the central IdP.
API Gateway + Spring Security Resource Servers protect APIs using Keycloak JWTs.

Architecture:

  Mobile / Web (Salam clients)
            ↓
       Keycloak Realm (salam)
         login → JWT
            ↓
      API Gateway
      (Spring Cloud Gateway / similar)
        - may validate JWT at edge
        - route to downstream services
            ↓
   ┌────────────┬─────────────┬────────────┐
   ↓            ↓             ↓            ↓
 user-svc   payment-svc   notify-svc   ...
 (Spring Security OAuth2 Resource Server)


Who does what?

Keycloak
  - authenticate user
  - issue access/refresh tokens
  - hold realm, clients, roles

API Gateway
  - single entry point for clients
  - routes /api/users → user-service, etc.
  - often validates Bearer JWT once at the edge
  - can reject unauthorized requests early (401/403)
  - may pass Authorization header downstream
  - optionally add internal headers after trust (careful with security)

Spring Security in each microservice (Resource Server)
  - spring-boot-starter-oauth2-resource-server
  - configured with Keycloak issuer URI, e.g.:
      spring.security.oauth2.resourceserver.jwt.issuer-uri=
        https://keycloak.../realms/salam
  - auto-fetches JWKS (public keys) from Keycloak
  - validates JWT on each request
  - @PreAuthorize("hasRole('ADMIN')") / hasAuthority(...) using token roles


Typical request path in Salam:

1) Client gets token from Keycloak
2) Client → Gateway:  Authorization: Bearer <jwt>
3) Gateway checks token (optional but common) + routes
4) Downstream Spring Boot service validates JWT again (defense in depth)
   OR trusts gateway-only validation in some internal setups
5) Method security uses roles from token


Custom JWT auth vs Salam Keycloak setup:

  Old/custom:
    Spring Boot /login → itself signs JWT → APIs validate with shared secret

  Salam + Keycloak:
    Keycloak signs JWT → Gateway + services validate with Keycloak public keys
    Users/roles managed in Keycloak admin, not only in app DB


Config idea (Spring Resource Server):

  spring:
    security:
      oauth2:
        resourceserver:
          jwt:
            issuer-uri: https://<keycloak-host>/realms/salam

  SecurityFilterChain:
    - authorizeHttpRequests
    - oauth2ResourceServer(jwt -> ...)


Gateway idea:
  - public routes: /actuator/health, maybe login redirects
  - all business routes require valid JWT
  - CORS / rate limits at gateway
  - forward Authorization header to services


