5) Diff: JWT vs Keycloak (END — remember this)
═══════════════════════════════════════

They are NOT competitors / not the same thing.

  JWT      → a TOKEN FORMAT
  Keycloak → an IAM / AUTH SERVER (product)

Analogy:
  JWT      → ticket paper (what the token looks like)
  Keycloak → ticket office + security system (issues & manages identity)


What it is
  JWT       → JSON Web Token: header.payload.signature
  Keycloak  → Identity & Access Management server (login, users, SSO, tokens)

Main job
  JWT       → carry claims (sub, roles, exp) in a signed string
  Keycloak  → authenticate users, manage realm/clients/roles, issue tokens

Protocol / standard
  JWT       → token format only (RFC 7519)
  Keycloak  → implements OAuth 2.0 + OpenID Connect (+ more)

Who creates the token?
  Custom JWT app → your Spring Boot /login signs it (HS256/RS256 you manage)
  Keycloak       → Keycloak issues access token (usually JWT)

User management
  JWT alone → your app DB / custom code
  Keycloak  → Keycloak admin + realm users (or LDAP/AD)

SSO / MFA / social login
  JWT alone → you build yourself
  Keycloak  → built-in features

Where used in Salam
  Keycloak  → central login / IAM
  JWT       → format of the access token that Gateway + Spring Security validate


Relationship (one line):
  Keycloak USES JWT.
  Keycloak ≠ replacement for JWT.
  JWT ≠ full auth system by itself.


When to say what in interview:
  “We use JWT for API authentication”     → talking about token format/flow
  “We use Keycloak for identity/SSO”      → talking about the auth server
  “Keycloak issues JWT access tokens”     → correct combined answer
